    <string name="privacy_loginHint">No ads, analytics or visit logs. Your sign-in key stays with you — the server keeps only its fingerprint, which cannot rebuild the key. Crash reports are anonymous.</string>
    <string name="privacy_moreLink">More about data →</string>
    <string name="privacy_contactLead">If something breaks, write to:</string>
    <string name="privacy_aboutTitle">Your data stays yours</string>
    <string name="privacy_aboutBody">No ads, analytics or email. Your name is optional: you sign in with a recovery key you control, and the server stores it only as a hash. The server keeps no logs about you. GreenThumb sends anonymous crash and freeze (ANR) reports and a session event at start, not linked to your account. Deleting your account removes your data at once; backup copies disappear as backups rotate.</string>
